{"type":"message","id":"27ef5d22","parentId":"a9c7a963","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:16:58.104Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read:27","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CABINET DIMENSIONS LEGEND\nIDENTIFICATION OF PARTS NOTES\nTYPICAL BLOCKING/ANCHORING LOCATION\nCASEWORK NOTES\nCONCRETE SLAB\nSTONHARD METAL COVE STRIP \n6\"\nSTONGLAZE VSM/COATING\nSTONHARD RTZ FLOORING\nCONCRETE SLAB\nSEALED CONCRETE\nDOOR AS SPECIFIED\nRESILIENT FLOORING\nRESILIENT REDUCER STRIP, \nMECHANICALLY FASTENED\nTROWELED HYDRAULIC CEMENT \nUNDERLAYMENT\n*TRANSITION DETAIL ONLY IF NEEDED WHERE CONCRETE DOESN'T ALIGN WITH EPOXY \nFLOORING.\n*IF EPOXY AND CONCRETE FLOOR ALIGN - BUTT JOIN\n2CM PORCELAIN WALL TILE\nSCHEDULED PARTITION \nTHIN SET MORTAR\nSCHLUTER - QUADEC\nTILE BACKER BOARD\nFULL HEIGHT CABINET \nBEYOND\nSCHEDULED PARTITION\n2CM PORCELAIN WALL TILE\nTHIN SET MORTAR BED\nSCHEDULED CEILING \nREFER TO \nPLAN\n1/8\" GROUT JOINT\nTHIN SET MORTAR BED\n2CM PORCELAIN WALL TILE\nSCHEDULED PARTITION. SKIM COAT AS \nREQ'D TO ENSURE 1/8\" TOLERANCE\n1/8\" GROUT JOINT\nCONCRETE SLAB\nSTONHARD METAL COVE STRIP \n6\"\nSTONHARD STONCLAD \nINTEGRAL BASE\nSTONHARD STONCLAD FLOORING\nSTONHARD STONEGLAZE WALL \nFINISH\nU.N.O. ON ELEVATIONS\nSEE CASEWORK DIMENSIONS LEGEND\nCENTERLINE OF DOOR PULL\n3'-2\"\nSEE PLAN\nCABINET PULL, SEE FINISH SCHEDULE\nWOOD BLOCKING AS \nREQUIRED\nPHENOLIC DOOR, 1\" THICK -\nLOCKABLE\nWOOD BLOCKING AS REQUIRED\n3\" MIN. #10 DIA. SCREW WITH A\nSURFACE BEARING HEAD MAX\nSPACING AT 16\" O.C. 6\" W X 16 GAUGE\nGALVANIZED STEEL PLATE SECURED TO\nA MINIMUM OF 3 STUDS WITH 2 #10\nSELF TAPPING SCREWS AT EACH STUD\nPHENOLIC SIDE PANEL\nPHENOLIC FASCIA\nSCRIBE\n1/2\"\n3\" MIN. #10 DIA. SCREW WITH A\nSURFACE BEARING HEAD MAX\nSPACING AT 16\" O.C. 6\" W X 16 GAUGE\nGALVANIZED STEEL PLATE SECURED TO\nA MINIMUM OF 3 STUDS WITH 2 #10\nSELF TAPPING SCREWS AT EACH STUD\nCONTINUOUS WOOD BLOCKING\nMELAMINE BACKER PANEL\nPROVIDE FLUSH MOUNTED\nCONCEALED HINGES FOR ALL CABINET\nDOORS\nCONTINUOUS WOOD BLOCKING\n2X4 WOOD BLOCKING\nCABINET PULL, SEE FINISH SCHEDULE\nPHENOLIC DOOR, 1\" THICK - LOCKABLE\nPHENOLIC SIDE PANEL\nPHENOLIC ADJUSTABLE SHELVING\nSCHEDULED BASE\nSEE PLANS\nSEE PLANS\n6\"\nGROUND FLOOR\n(ACTUAL 1ST\nFLOOR)\n13' - 1 1/2\"\nMTL RUNNER\nPHENOLIC PANEL\nHORIZONTAL STEEL MEMBER, PER \nSTRUCT DWGS\nSEALANT B/W SOLID SURFACE & WINDOW FRAME\nSOLID SURFACE SILL\nSOLID SURFACE COUNTERTOP\nCOUNTER SUPPORT BRACKET\nSHIM WINDOW AS REQUIRED\nACCESS PANEL @36\" MAX \nFOR WIRE MANAGEMENT\n3' - 6\"\n2' - 6\"\n7/16\" FIBERGLASS BALLISTIC PANELS\n1/2\" CEMENT BOARD\nTHINSET PER MANUFACTURER'S RECOMMENDATIONS\nTILE WALL PANEL, PER FINISH SCHEDULE\nBLOCKING FOR COUNTERTOP BRACKET\nBLOCKING FOR COUNTERTOP BRACKET\nMTL STUD @ 16\" O.C.\nMTL RUNNER\nTILE WALL PANEL, PER \nFINISH SCHEDULE\nMTL STUD, @ 16\" O.C.\nTHIN SET PER MANUFACTURER'S \nRECOMENDATION\nSCHLUTER TRIM PER FINISH \nSCHEDULE\n1/2\" CEMENT BOARD\n7/16\" FIBERGLASS BALLISTIC PANEL\nPHENOLIC PANEL SECURED \nTO WOOD BLOCK, PROVIDE \nACCESS PANELS @ 36\" FOR \nWIRE MANAGEMENT \nWITHIN MILL WORK\n1. \nCONTRACTOR TO FIELD VERIFY ALL DIMENSIONS BEFORE FABRICATION.\n2. \nDIMENSIONS IDENTIFIED IN THE THIS LEGEND ARE TYPICAL UNLESS \nOTHERWISE NOTED IN ELEVATIONS AND OR SECTIONS.\nWORK COUNTER\nFULL HEIGHT CABINETS\nFULL HEIGHT \nCABINET\nSHELVES SEE \nCASEWORK NOTES\nFASCIA/SOFFIT\nCEILING\nBACK SPLASH\nWALL BRACKET\nSEE CASEWORK \nNOTES\nA. 2'-6\" TYPICAL \n2'-1\" WHEN ADJACENT \nTO BASE CABINETS\nB. 2'-6\"\nA. 1'-1\" TO 2'-1\" (SEE PLAN)\nB. 11\"\nC. 4\"\nD. 3\"\nE. \n5'-6\" TYPICAL\n3'-10\" ADA COMPLIANT  \nF. \n2\"\nG. 7'-2\"\n1. \nEXPOSED PARTS - SURFACES VISIBLE WHEN:\nA. FRONT OF DRAWERS AND DOORS ARE IN CLOSED POSITION.\nB. SHELVES ARE IN OPEN TYPE CABINETS AND OR SHELVES ARE \nBEHIND CLEAR GLASS DOORS.\nC. BOTTOMS OF CABINETS AREA LOCATED 42\" OR MORE ABOVE \nFINISHED FLOOR.\nD. TOP OF CABINETS IS VISIBLE OR CAN BE SEEN FROM UPPER FLOOR \nOR STAIRCASE.\nE. \nPORTION OF CABINETS ARE VISIBLE AFTER FIXED APPLIANCES ARE \nINSTALLED.\nF. \nFRONT EDGES OF CABINET PARTS ARE VISIBLE OR CAN BE SEEN \nTHROUGH A GAP GREATER THAN 1/8\" WITH CABINET DOORS AND \nDRAWERS ARE IN CLOSED POSITION.\n2. \nSEMI-EXPOSED PARTS - SURFACES VISIBLE WHEN:\n3. \nDRAWER AND DOORS ARE IN OPEN POSITION.\n4. \nBOTTOMS OF CABINETS ARE LOCATED AT 30\" AND UP TO 42\" ABOVE \nFINISHED FLOOR.\n5. \nALL FRONT EDGES OF SHELVING ARE BEHIND DOORS.\n6. \nCONCEALED SURFACES - SURFACES ARE CONCEALED WHEN:\nA. SURFACES ARE NOT VISIBLE AFTER INSTALLATION.\nB. BOTTOMS OF CABINETS ARE LOCATED AT OR LESS THAN 30\" ABOVE \nFINISHED FLOOR.\nC. TOPS OF CABINETS ARE LOCATED AT OR OVER 78\" ABOVE FINISHED \nFLOOR AND ARE NOT VISIBLE FROM AN UPPER FLOOR OR \nSTAIRCASE.\nD. STRETCHERS, BLOCKING AND/OR COMPONENTS ARE CONCEALED \nBY DRAWERS\nVARIES\nG\nE\nF\nB\nA\nD\nC\nA\nB\n* VERIFY ALL DIMENSIONS WITH CASEWORK CONTRACTOR. BLOCKING \nHEIGHT MAY VARY DEPENDING ON CABINET HEIGHT, COUNTER TOP HEIGHT \n& FIELD CONDITIONS\nA\nC\n2'-6\"\n7'-2\"\nB\nA. 7'-4\" TYP.\nB. 5'-0\" FOR 30\" UPPER CABINETS\n5'-6\" FOR 24\" UPPER CABINETS\n4'-6\" FOR 36\" UPPER CABINETS\nC. 2'-10 1/2\" TYP.\nWORK COUNTER\nFINISH FLOOR\nVARIES\n6\"\nTOP OF \nCOUNTER\n1. \nTHESE NOTES ARE TYPICAL UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED.\n2. \nALL CASEWORK TO BE BALANCED CONSTRUCTION.\n3. \nALL COUNTERTOPS WITH SINKS TO HAVE MOISTURE RESISTANT MDF \nSUBSTRATE.\n4. \nALL EXPOSED AND SEMI EXPOSED PARTS, AS DETERMINED IN THE \n\"IDENTIFICATION OF PART NOTES\" TO HAVE PLASTIC LAMINATE FINISH.\n5. \nALL SIX FACES OF ADJUSTABLE SHELVING TO HAVE PLASTIC LAMINATE \nFINISH.\n6. \nALL ADJUSTABLE SHELVING TO BE 12\" DEEP UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED\n7. \nALL SHELVES TO BE 3/4\" THICK MDF FOR SPANS UP TO 3'-0\". ADD 3/4\" X \n1-1/2\" SOLID LUMBER DROPPED EDGE FOR SPANS OVER 3'-0\".\n8. \nALL OPEN SPACE SIZES AND KNEE BRACES LOCATIONS TO BE VERIFIED \nWITH EQUIPMENT TO BE INSTALLED AND WITH ACTUAL ROOM \nDIMENSIONS.\n9. \nCOUNTERTOPS TO RECEIVE A 2\" X 2\" CONTINUOUS METAL ANGLE AT \nALL WALL LOCATIONS.\n10. PROVIDE SURFACE MOUNTED WALL BRACKET FOR COUNTERS WITH \nSPANS GREATER THAN 2'-8\" UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\n11. ALL PLASTIC LAMINATE JOINTS TO BE NOTED ON SHOP DRAWINGS.\n12. 4\" BACKSPLASH AND ENDSPLASH TYPICAL UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED.\n13. ALL FINISHED END PANELS AT WALL CABINETS TO BE ONE CONTINUOUS \nPANEL INCLUDING VALANCE.\n14. ALL FINISHED END PANELS AT BASE CABINETS TO BE ONE CONTINUOUS \nPANEL INCLUDING BASE.\n15. ALL FILE CABINETS TO HAVE MINIMUM CLEAR DIMENSIONS TO ACCEPT \nSTANDARD PENDAFLEX FILE FRAME.\n16. ALL EXPOSED CORNERS OF COUNTERTOPS TO HAVE 1/2\" RADIUS.\n17. AT CUTOUTS AND \"L\" SHAPED COUNTERTOPS, ALL INSIDE CORNERS TO \nBE SMOOTHLY ROUNDED WITH A MINIMUM CORNER RADIUS OF 1/2\".\n18. INSTALL GROMMETS IN COUNTER TOPS AT 3'-0\" ON CENTER.\n19. ALL WALL CABINETS TO HAVE VALANCE UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\n20. IN EXISTING PARTITION WHERE METAL PLATE IS REQUIRED TO SUPPORT \nCABINETS, REMOVE SECTION OF EXISTING GYPSUM WALL BOARD TO \nINSTALL METAL PLATE. PATCH WALL WITH GYPSUM WALLBOARD TO AN \nEVEN SURFACE TO MATCH EXISTING. \n21. PROVIDE A MINIMUM 1-1/2\" FILLER / SCRIBE STRIPS AT JUNCTION \nBETWEEN ALL BASE AND WALL CABINETS AND ADJACENT WALLS TO \nALLOW DOORS TO SWING OPEN AT LEAST 90 DEGREES.\n22. AT EXISTING PARTITION PROVIDE 1/2\" SCRIBE AT TOP AND SIDE OF \nSIDESPLASH AND AT TOP OF BACKSPLASH FOR WALL TOLERANCE.\n23. ALL FLOORING TO CONTINUE UNDER ALL CASEWORK.\n24. ALL CABINETRY TO BE LOCKABLE.\n2'-10\"\n6\" 16 GAUGE \nCONTINUOUS METAL \nPLATE FASTENED TO A \nMINIMUM OF 3 STUDS \n6\" 16 GAUGE \nCONTINUOUS METAL \nPLATE\n6\" 20 GAUGE METAL \nRUNNER \n200 MADISON AVENUE, 14TH FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY 10016\n212-689-3110\nARRAY-ARCHITECTS.COM\nPROJECT NO.\nDATE\nCONTRACT NO.\nCON/REF NO.\nF\nE\nD\nC\nB\nA\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n3\n2\n1\nC  COPYRIGHT - 2025 ARRAY ARCHITECTS\nIN COLLABORATION WITH:\nDOSHI ENGINEERING PLLC\nMEP ENGINEER\n350 SEVENTH AVENUE, 15th FLOOR,\nNEW YORK, NY 10001\nPHONE: 718 896 9324\nPROJECT:\nISSUES:\nSEAL:\nKEYPLAN:\nYSRAEL A. SEINUK, P.C.\nSTRUCTURAL ENGINEER\n228 EAST 45TH STREET, 2ND FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY  10017\nPHONE: 212 687 2233\nYU & ASSOCIATES\nGEOTECHNICAL & CIVIL ENGINEER\n611 RIVER DRIVE\nELMWOOD PARK, NY  07407\nPHONE: 201 791 0057\nMG ENGINEERING D.P.C.\nMEDICAL EQ, AV/IT, SECURITY ENGINEER\n116 WEST 32ND STREET\nNEW YORK, NY  10001\nPHONE: 212 643 9055  \nENVIRONMENTAL PLANNING \nMANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER\n1983 MARCUS AVENUE, SUITE 109\nLAKE SUCCESS, NY  11042\nPHONE: 516 328 1194 \n9/25/2025 10:53:59 AM\nAutodesk Docs://6829 - H+H Bellevue Ambulance Bay Addition/6829-ARCH- ED ADDITION-25.rvt\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n09/25/25 A-702 .00\nCASEWORK AND\nINTERIOR DETAILS\nED AMBULANCE\nBAY ADDITION\nH+H Bellevue\n6829\n09/25/25\n462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\nISSUED SOLTUION FOR BID 2025\n3\" = 1'-0\"\nA3\nSTONHARD RTZ BASE\n3\" = 1'-0\"\nA5\nSECTION @ EPOXY FLOOR TO CONCRETE\n3\" = 1'-0\"\nA7\nPT/W-1 WALL TILE: OUTSIDE CORNER DETAIL\n6\" = 1'-0\"\nA8\nFULL HEIGHT PT/W-1 PANEL - TILE TOP DETAIL\n6\" = 1'-0\"\nB3\nFULL HEIGHT PT/W-1 PANEL - VERTICAL JOINT DETAIL\n3\" = 1'-0\"\nA4\nSTONHARD STONCLAD BASE\n1 1/2\" = 1'-0\"\nC4\nSECTION @ FULL HEIGHT CABINET\n1 1/2\" = 1'-0\"\nD3\nSECTION @ TYPICAL BASE CABINET\n3\" = 1'-0\"\nC8\nSECURITY CONTROL DESK SECTION DETAIL\n3\" = 1'-0\"\nE3\nSECURITY DESK CORNER DETAIL\nNO. DESCRIPTION\nDATE\n1\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n09/25/25\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052618102}}
