TESTS TO BE PERFORMED\nPOST INSTALLED ADHESIVE ANCHORS (BB# 2014-018, 2014-019)\nBC 1705.37\nWALL PANELS, CURTAIN WALLS & VENEERS\nBC 1705.20\nDEEP FOUNDATION ELEMENTS (TR5)\nBC 1705.7\nSUBSURFACE CONDITIONS - FILL PLACEMENT & IN PLACE DENSITY\nBC 1705.6\nSUBGRADE INSPECTION\nBC 1705.6\nMASONRY\nBC 1705.54\nCONCRETE SAMPLING AND TESTING TR2 ONLY\nBC 1905.2-1905.6.5\nCONCRETE- CAST-IN PLACE\nBC 1705.3\nSTRUCTURAL STEEL - HIGH STRENGTH BOLTS\nBC 1704.3.3\nSTRUCTURAL STEEL - DETAILS BC\nBC 1705.2.2\nSTRUCTURAL STEEL - WELDING\nBC 1705.2.1\nTHE \"AUTHORITY\" SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR THE FOLLOWING SPECIAL INSPECTIONS:\n72 HOURS BEFORE THE SPECIFIC WORK COMMENCES\nTHE CONTRACTOR MUST NOTIFY THE SPECIAL INPSECTION AGENCY FOR SPECIAL INSPECTIONS AT LEAST\nNYC CONSTRUCTION CODE ARE LISTED IN THE FOLLOWING TABLES:\nSPECIAL INSPECTIONS REQUIRED IN ACCORDANCE WITH CHAPTER 17 AND THE APPLICABLE SECTIONS OF THE\nSPECIAL INSPECTIONS\nNO.\nDESCRIPTION\nDATE\n1\n95% Solution\n6/20/2025\nDRAWING LIST.\nSheet Number\nSheet Name\nFO-001\nFOUNDATION - COVER SHEET AND DRAWING LIST\nFO-002\nFOUNDATION GENERAL NOTES\nFO-101\nFOUNDATION PLAN\nFO-200\nTYPICAL FOUNDATION DETAILS\nFO-201\nTYPICAL FOUNDATION DETAILS\nFO-300\nFOUNDATION SECTIONS\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID     7/18/25\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052632432}}
{"type":"message","id":"d086f625","parentId":"735f8dd9","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:12.437Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read:34","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"EXCAVATION\n1. \nBUILDING LOADS SHALL BE SUPPORTED ON ##### KIP CAPACITY PILES WITH ##.##\" DIAMETER X 0.###\" THICK \nCASING.\n2. \nALL PILES WITHIN +/- 30'-0\" OF EXISTING STRUCTURE TO BE DRILLED, SEE PLAN FOR DRILLED PILE LOCATIONS.\n3. \nCONTRACTOR TO COORDINATE THE CHANGES IN LOCATIONS OF PILE CAPS AND WALLS WHERE IMPACTED BY \nEXISTING PIER AND FOOTING LOCATIONS, AND TO LAYOUT IN-FIELD THE NEW PILE CAP AND WALL LOCATION AS \nDIRECTED BY ENGINEER AND AUTHORITY.\n4. \nWHERE A PIER IS INDICATED ON THE FOUNDATION PLAN BUT ELIMINATED IN THE FIELD THE ENGINEER SHALL BE \nNOTIFIED AS THE DEPTH OF PILE CAP MAY NEED TO BE INCREASED.\n5. \nALL EXCAVATIONS SHOULD BE CONDUCTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH ALL OSHA REQUIREMENTS INCLUDING, BUT \nNOT LIMITED TO, TEMPORARY SHORING, UTILIZING TRENCH BOXES, AND PROPER BENCHING. ALL WORK PLANS \nSHOULD BE SUBMITTED FOR AUTHORITY AND DESIGN TEAM REVIEW PRIOR TO COMMENCEMENT OF EXCAVATION \nOPERATIONS.\n6. \nSEE SITE SURVEY DRAWING, DEMOLITION PLAN, LANDSCAPE DRAWINGS, PLUMBING DRAWINGS, \nARCHITECTURAL, MECHANICAL, AND ELECTRICAL DRAWINGS FOR PROPOSED AND EXISTING UNDERGROUND \nUTILITIES.\n7. \nCONSTRUCTION DE-WATERING MAY BE NEEDED DURING THE EXCAVATION FOR FOUNDATIONS AND UTILITY \nEXCAVATIONS. CARE SHOULD BE TAKEN TO ENSURE THAT DRAINAGE IS PROVIDED DURING ALL PHASES OF THE \nPROJECT;THE EARTHWORK CONTRACTOR MUST TAKE WHATEVER STEPS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE \nGENERAL SUBGRADE IN A WORKABLE CONDITION NEW YORK CITY DEPARTMENT OF ENVIRONMENTAL \nPROTECTION (DEP) REQUIRES THAT AN ESTIMATE OF GROUNDWATER DISCHARGE PERMIT. ENVIRONMENTAL \nTESTING OF THE GROUNDWATER MAY BE REQUIRED. THE CONTRACTOR SHOULD PROVIDE A SUBMISSION \nPREPARED BY A PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER REGISTERED IN THE STATE OF NEW YORK ON THE PROPOSED MEANS \nAND METHODS FOR TEMPORARY DE-WATERING.\n8. \nGROUND WATER LEVELS SHOULD BE MAINTAINED AT LEAST 2 FT BELOW THE PROPOSED FOUNDATIONS \nSUBGRADE DURING EXCAVATION AND FOUNDATION CONSTRUCTION.\n9. \nWHERE EXISTING PILECAP FOUNDATION OF ADJACENT PROPERTY IS LOWER THAN ELEVATIONS SHOWN NEW \nFOUNDATIONS ARE TO BE LOWERED TO SAME ELEVATION. WHERE NEW FOUNDATION IS LOWER THAN EXISTING \nFOUNDATIONS, CONTRACTORS IS TO UNDERPIN EXISTING FOUNDATION. CONTRACTOR IS TO ESTABLISH \nEXISTING CONDITIONS BEFORE COMMENCING WORK AND NOTIFY THE ENGINEER.\nCODES AND TESTS\n1. \nTHE STRUCTURE HAS BEEN DESIGNED UNDER THE PROVISIONS OF THE 2022 NYS BUILDING CODE AND A.C.I.\n2. \nIN CONFORMANCE WITH THE BUILDING CODE, THE AUTHORITY WILL ASSIGN A LICENSED PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER, \nAPPROVED BY THE ENGINEER OF RECORD, TO SUPERVISE THE TESTING OF THE MATERIALS AND THE INSPECTION \nOF CONCRETE CONSTRUCTION AND TO CHECK THAT ALL REQUIRED TESTS ARE MADE AND LABORATORY TESTS ARE \nSUBMITTED. THE ENGINEER SHALL HAVE THE RIGHT TO ORDER THE CONTRACTOR TO MAKE SUCH CHANGES OF THE \nMIX OF CONCRETE AS REQUIRED TO PRODUCE CONCRETE OF THE NECESSARY STRENGTH AND TO REPORT TO THE \nBUILDING DEPARTMENT SUPERINTENDENT ANY DEVIATION FROM THE REQUIREMENTS OF THE CODE AS INDICATED \nBY RECORDS OF INSPECTION AND REPORTS OF TEST.\n3. \nDESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION OF FORMWORK IS TO COMPLY WITH THE A.C.I. AND NYS BUILDING CODE AS AMENDED.\n4. \nALL EARTH WORK INCLUDING EXCAVATION, FILLING, AND SUBGRADE PREPARATION SHALL BE IN CONFORMANCE \nWITH THE SPECIFICATIONS AND GEOTECHNICAL INVESTIGATIONS PREPARED BY ####; DATED ##/##/####.\n5. \nALL MATERIAL FABRICATION, INSTALLATION AND INSPECTION REQUIREMENTS RELATING TO FOUNDATIONS SHALL \nCONFORM TO THE BUILDING CODE.\nANCHOR BOLTS SPECIFICATION\n1. \nANCHOR BOLTS (ANCHOR RODS): SHALL CONFORM TO THE PROVISIONS OF ASTM F1554, GRADE 36, UNLESS \nDIFFERENT GRADE IS SPECIFIED ELSEWHERE. SIZE AND DETAILING INDICATED ON DRAWINGS.\n2. \nDELIVER ANCHOR BOLTS AND OTHER ANCHORAGE DEVICES, WHICH ARE TO BE EMBEDDED IN CAST-IN-PLACE \nCONCRETE OR MASONRY, IN AMPLE TIME SO AS NOT TO DELAY WORK.\n3. \na)  FURNISH TO THE CONCRETE AND BRICK MASONS ANCHOR BOLTS AND OTHER CONNECTORS REQUIRED \nFOR SECURING STRUCTURAL STEEL TO THE FOUNDATION AND OTHER IN-PLACE  CONCRETE WORK, \nTOGETHER WITH INSTRUCTIONS, TEMPLATES, ETC. NECESSARY FOR SETTING THEM. ANCHOR BOLTS ARE TO \nBE SURVEYED AND ANY APPROVED MODIFICATIONS MADE PRIOR TO PLACEMENT OF COLUMNS.\nb) TIGHTEN ANCHOR BOLTS AFTER SUPPORT MEMBERS HAVE BEEN POSITIONED AND PLUMBED. CUT OFF \nPROTRUDING EDGES OF WEDGES OR SHIMS FLUSH WITH EDGE OF BASE OR BEARING PLATE PRIOR TO \nPACKING WITH GROUT.\nMISCELLANEOUS NOTES\n1. \nPERFORM REMOVAL WORK TO PREPARE THE PROPOSED LOCATION FOR THE FOUNDATION I.E. REMOVAL OF TREES, \nSTUMPS, SHRUBS, CONCRETE SLABS, ASPHALT PAVING, CATCH BASINS, YARD DRAINS, PLAYGROUND EQUIPMENT, \nFLAG AND UTILITY POLES, ETC.\n2. \nTOTAL AND DIFFERENTIAL COLUMN SETTLEMENTS ARE EXPECTED TO BE LESS THAN ## INCH AND ## INCHES \nRESPECTIVELY. THE MAJORITY OF SETTLEMENTS ARE EXPECTED TO OCCUR DURING CONSTRUCTION. THESE \nSETTLEMENTS SHOULD BE WITHIN TOLERABLE LIMITS OF A CONVENTIONAL REINFORCED CONCRETE OR STEEL FRAME \nSTRUCTURE.\n3. \nFOUNDATION: MONITORING BUILDINGS ON THE SAME LOT OR A NEIGHBORING LOT IS IN COMPLIANCE WITH CHAPTER \n33 OF THE NYSBC WHEN GOING BELOW 5' IN DEPTH, HISTORIC STRUCTURES WITH 90' OR BUILDINGS WITHIN A \nDISTANCE EQUAL OR LESS THAN THE DEPTH OF EXCAVATION OR WHEN IMPOSING LOADS. \"CONTRACTOR'S NY STATE \nLICENSED ENGINEER TO ISSUE MONITORING PLAN PRIOR TO PERMIT. ACTUAL MONITORING  TO BE COMPLETED BY \nCONTRACTOR FOR DURATION OF PROJECT SCHEDULE\".\n4. \nTEMPORARY BRACING SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR ALL BUTTRESSES WHERE BUTTRESSES DO NOT EXIST OR SPACING \nBETWEEN BUTTRESSES IS GREATER THAN 25 FEET. TEMPORARY BRACING SHALL BE PROVIDED WHERE THE \nDIFFERENCES IN LEVEL BETWEEN INSIDE AND OUTSIDE GRADE IS GREATER THAN 4'-0\". CORNER BUTTRESSES DO NOT \nREQUIRE BRACING. NO BACKFILLING IS TO BE DONE BEFORE ALL SLABS BRACING WALLS ARE IN PLACE UNLESS \nAPPROVED BY EOR.\n5. \nWATER SHALL NOT BE ALLOWED TO STAND IN TRENCHES BEFORE OR AFTER CONCRETE IS PLACED. IF TRENCHES \nBECOME SOFT DUE TO RAIN OR OTHER WATER BEFORE FOOTINGS OR PITS ARE CAST, THE CONTRACTOR SHOULD \nEXCAVATE THE SOFTENED MATERIAL AND REPLACE WITH CONCRETE.\n6. \nAll DESIGNS OF ON-SITE CONSTRUCTION INCLUDING RAMPS, STEPS, ETC. ARE TO BE REVIEWED AND APPROVED BY \nTHE LOCAL AUTHORITY.\nEARTHWORK NOTES\n1. ALL EARTH WORK INCLUDING EXCAVATION, FILLING, AND SUBGRADE PREPARATION SHALL BE IN CONFORMANCE WITH \nTHE SPECIFICATIONS AND GEOTECHNICAL INVESTIGATIONS PREPARED BY #######, DATED ##/##/2025  REQUIREMENTS \nCONTAINED IN THE GEOTECH INVESTIGATION ARE PART OF THIS WORK.\n2. ALL MATERIAL, FABRICATION, INSTALLATION AND INSPECTION REQUIREMENTS RELATING TO FOUNDATIONS SHALL \nCONFORM TO THE BUILDING CODE. \n3. THE CONTRACTOR IS SOLELY RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL EXCAVATION PROCEDURES INCLUDING LAGGING, SHORING, AND \nPROTECTION OF ADJACENT PROPERTY, STRUCTURES, STREETS, AND UTILITIES IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE \nREQUIREMENTS OF THE LOCAL BUILDING DEPARTMENT AND OSHA REGULATIONS. DO NOT EXCAVATE WITHIN ONE \nFOOT OF THE ANGLE OF REPOSE OF ANY SOIL BEARING FOUNDATION UNLESS THE FOUNDATION IS PROPERLY \nPROTECTED AGAINST SETTLEMENT.\n4. BACKFILLING AT RETAINING WALLS SHALL BE DONE IN SUCH A MANNER THAT THE DIFFERENCE IN GRADES ON EITHER \nSIDE OF THE WALL SHALL NOT EXCEED 2 FEET AT ANY STAGE OF BACKFILLING UNTIL THE CONTRACT GRADES ARE \nREACHED. THE QUALIFIED SOIL INSPECTOR AND PROJECT STRUCTURAL ENGINEER SHALL BE NOTIFIED 48-HOURS IN \nADVANCE PRIOR TO ANY BACKFILLING OF RETAINING WALLS\n5. SEE CIVIL/LANDSCAPE ARCHITECTURE AND ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS FOR SCOPE OF WORK BEYOND FOOT PRINT \nOF THE BUILDING.\n6. EXCAVATIONS BELOW FOOTINGS OF ALL TYPES AS WELL AS SLABS ON GRADE SHOULD BE MADE SO AS TO PROVIDE A \nCLEAN EVEN BEARING AREA AND SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE SPECIFICATIONS AND THE GEOTECH. REPORT.\n7. CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR DISPOSAL OF ALL ACCUMULATED WATER IN A MANNER THAT DOES NOT \nINCONVENIENCE OR DAMAGE THE WORK.\n8. ALL UNDERPINNING, SHEETING, SHORING OR OTHER CONSTRUCTION REQUIRED FOR THE SUPPORT OF ADJACENT \nPROPERTIES, BUILDINGS, SIDEWALKS, UTILITIES, ETC. SHALL BE SUBJECT TO SPECIAL INSPECTION AS REQUIRED BY \nTHE CODE. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL RETAIN A LICENSED PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER ACCEPTABLE TO THE ENGINEER \nOF RECORD TO PROVIDE THE NECESSARY DESIGN AND THE REQUIRED INSPECTION. THE CONTRACTOR'S \nPROFESSIONAL ENGINEER SHALL PREPARE AND FILE THE REQUIRED FORMS FOR THE WORK WITH THE BUILDING \nDEPARTMENT\n9. THE REMOVAL WORK TO PREPARE THE PROPOSED LOCATION FOR THE FOUNDATION I.E. REMOVAL OF TREES, \nSTUMPS, SHRUBS, CONCRETE SLABS, ASPHALT PAVING, CATCH BASINS, YARD DRAINS, PLAYGROUND EQUIPMENT, \nFLAG AND UTILITY POLES, ETC. IS THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE CONTRACTOR.\n10. CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE A SURVEY OF THE ADJACENT BUILDING AND TO SUBMIT THE SURVEY IMMEDIATELY TO THE \nENGINEER OF RECORD AND THE AUTHORITY. \n11. WHERE EXISTING FOOTING OR FOUNDATION OF ADJACENT PROPERTY IS LOWER THAN ELEVATIONS SHOWN, NEW \nFOUNDATIONS ARE TO BE LOWERED TO MATCH WITH THE ELEVATION OF EXISTING FOUNDATION; WHERE NEW \nFOUNDATION IS LOWER THAN  EXISTING FOUNDATIONS, CONTRACTOR IS TO UNDERPIN EXISTING FOUNDATION PER \nSUGGESTED DETAIL. CONTRACTOR IS TO ESTABLISH EXISTING CONDITIONS BEFORE COMMENCING WORK AND NOTIFY \nTHE ENGINEER.\n12. WHERE EXCAVATION WILL EXTEND MORE THAN 10'-0\" BELOW THE LEGALLY ESTABLISHED GRADE, THE DETAILS OF \nUNDERPINNING AND/OR BRACING REQUIRED FOR THE SUPPORT OF ADJACENT BUILDINGS OR PROPERTIES SHALL BE \nPREPARED BY A PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER HIRED BY THE CONTRACTOR. SEE SPECIFICATIONS.\nFOUNDATION NOTES\n1. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL COMPACT SUBGRADE, AND PREPARE WITH VAPOR BARRIER AND DENSE GRADED \nAGGREGATE UNDER THE STRUCTURE SLAB. SEE \"EARTHWORK\" SPECIFICATIONS FOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION. SEE \nARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS FOR WATERPROOFING REQUIREMENTS.\n2. MAINTAIN GROUND WATER LEVEL A MINIMUM OF 2 FEET BELOW EXCAVATION DURING CONSTRUCTION. CONTRACTOR \nIS TO VERIFY GROUND WATER LEVEL. CONTRACTOR IS FULLY RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DE-WATERING DURING \nCONSTRUCTION REGARDLESS OF THE LEVEL OF GROUND WATER.\n3. WATER SHALL NOT BE ALLOWED TO STAND IN TRENCHES BEFORE OR AFTER CONCRETE IS PLACED. IF TRENCHES \nBECOME SOFTENED DUE TO RAIN OR OTHER WATER BEFORE THE FOOTINGS ARE CAST, THE CONTRACTOR SHALL \nEXCAVATE THE SOFTENED MATERIAL AND REPLACE WITH CONCRETE.\n4. EXCAVATION AND STRUCTURAL FILL COMPACTION TO BE CARRIED OUT IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE GEOTECH. REPORT \nAND SPECIFICATION. ALL EXCAVATIONS AND SUBGRADE BEARING LEVELS FOR FOUNDATIONS SHALL BE APPROVED BY \nAN INDEPENDENT TESTING AGENCY OR SITE REPRESENTATIVE PRIOR TO CASTING OF CONCRETE.\n5. ALL BEARING SURFACES SHALL BE PROTECTED FROM CHANGES IN MOISTURE CONTENT IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE \nFOUNDATION REPORT AND SPECIFICATIONS.\n6. ALL FOUNDATIONS ARE TO BE FORMED AND CENTERED ON COLUMNS ABOVE AS SHOWN ON DRAWINGS. PROVIDE \nDOWELS IN PILE CAPS FOR CONNECTION TO SLAB, WALLS, OF SAME NUMBER AND SIZE AS THE VERTICAL \nREINFORCEMENT ABOVE, U.N.O.\n7. PROVIDE CONCRETE ENCASEMENT FOR ALL STEEL THAT WOULD OTHERWISE BE EXPOSED TO EARTH IN ITS FINAL \nCONDITION U.N.O. MINIMUM CONCRETE COVER SHALL BE 4\".\n8. ALL LOAM, LOOSE SOIL FILL AND LOOSE SAND BELOW AND WITHIN 1'-0\" OF THE FOOTPRINT OF THE BUILDING ARE NOT \nSUITABLE FOR FOUNDATION AND SLAB ON GRADE SUPPORT AND MUST BE ENTIRELY REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH \nCONTROLLED COMPACTED STRUCTURAL FILL. COMPACTED STRUCTURAL FILL SHALL CONSIST OF ACCEPTABLE ON-\nSITE / OFF SITE SOILS, AS APPROVED BY THE INSPECTING SOIL'S ENGINEER, COMPACTED TO A MINIMUM OF 95% OF ITS \nMAXIMUM DRY DENSITY AS DETERMINED BY THE MODIFIED PROCTOR TEST (ASTM-D1557). THE CONTROLLED FILL \nMATERIAL SHALL HAVE NO MORE THAN 10% BY WEIGHT PASSING # 200 SIEVES.\n9. PILE CAPS CAN BE LOWERED , NOTCHED, INCREASED IN THICKNESS OR ALTERED IN AN APPROPRIATE MANNER TO \nACCOMMODATE MECHANICAL SERVICE LINES, PENDING APPROVAL FROM THE STRUCTURAL ENGINEER OF RECORD.\nA. ECCENTRICITIES OF PILE GROUPS SHALL BE ADJUSTED BY STRAPS, ADDITIONAL REINFORCING OR BY THE \nDRILLING OF ADDITIONAL PILES AND INDICATED ON REDESIGN SHEETS AS PREPARED BY THE STRUCTURAL \nENGINEER.\nB. DURING PILE INSTALLATION OPERATIONS PILE CONTRACTOR SHALL MONITOR EXISTING BUILDINGS AT LOT LINES \nAND TAKE NECESSARY MEASURES TO PROTECT EXISTING BUILDINGS, INCLUDING AUGERING PILES AS REQUIRED \nAVOIDING ANY DISPLACEMENT OF MATERIALS.\nC. PILES SHALL CONSIST OF DRILLED PILES WITHIN 30 FEET OF EXISTING STRUCTURES  AS SHOWN IN THESE \nDRAWINGS. REFER TO SPECIFICATION ## ## ## AND ## ## ##. SELECTED DRILLED PILE DESIGN SHALL BE PROVIDED \nBY THE CONTRACTOR FOR REVIEW BY THE AUTHORITY'S ENGINEER. TWO SACRIFICIAL DRILLED PILES SHALL BE \nINSTALLED AND LOAD TESTED IN COMPRESSION AND TENSION PRIOR TO THE CONSTRUCTION OF PRODUCTION \nPILES. \n10. STRUCTURAL SLAB ON GRADE:\nA. WELDED WIRE MESH OR REINFORCING BARS SHALL BE SUPPORTED ON HIGH CHAIRS TO AVOID DISPLACEMENT. \nB. WELDED PLAIN WIRE FABRIC SHALL CONFORM TO \"SPECIFICATION FOR WELDED STEEL-WIRE FABRIC FOR \nCONCRETE REINFORCEMENT\" (ASTM A185) AND HAVE A MINIMUM YIELD STRENGTH OF 60,000 PSI.\nC. FOR TYPE OF FLOOR FINISH, SEE ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS AND SPECIFICATIONS. THE FLOOR SLABS SHALL BE \nDEPRESSED AS REQUIRED, SEE DETAILS. THE BOLTS FOR MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT SHALL BE PLACED BEFORE \nTHE CONCRETE IS POURED.\nD. FOR EXTERIOR CONCRETE EXPOSED TO DEICING SALT AND FREEZE THAW, DESIGN CRITERIA LISTED IN BUILDING \nCODE, ACI 318, TABLE 19.3.2.1, SHALL BE COMPLIED WITH AIR ENTRAINED, f'c=4500 PSI, W/C=0.45 WITH 15-20% CLASS \nF FLY ASH CEMENTITIOUS MATERIAL.\nE. SLABS SHALL BE FLAT & LEVEL PER SPECIFICATIONS; BUT NOT LESS THAN THE FOLLOWING UNLESS WRITTEN \nAPPROVAL IS  RECEIVED FROM ARCHITECT:\na. 10.5.2. SLAB ON GRADE: FF 25 / FL 20.\nCONCRETE AND STEEL REINFORCEMENT NOTES\n1. ALL CONCRETE WORK SHALL BE IN CONFORMANCE WITH THE SPECIFICATION SECTION 03200 AND 03300, AND \nAMERICAN CONCRETE INSTITUTE \"BUILDING CODE REQUIREMENTS FOR STRUCTURAL CONCRETE\" ACI 318-14 (ACI).\nA. \"ACI MANUAL OF CONCRETE PRACTICE\" - PART 1 TO 6, BY AMERICAN CONCRETE INSTITUTE.\nB. \"MANUAL OF STANDARD PRACTICE\" BY CRSI.\nC. \"ACI DETAILING MANUAL\" BY ACI.\n2. NO CONCRETE FOOTING, FOUNDATION PIER, OR FOUNDATION WALL SHALL BE PLACED UNTIL SUBGRADE FOR SAME \nHAS BEEN APPROVED BY A LICENSED PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER. \n3. ALL CONCRETE SHALL BE NORMAL WEIGHT CONTROLLED CONCRETE (U.O.N) AND COMPLY WITH THE BUILDING CODE, \nPROJECT SPECIFICATIONS, ACI 301, AND ACI 318. APPLICATION FOR CONTROLLED CONCRETE WITH CONCRETE DESIGN \nMIX PREPARED BY AN APPROVED LABORATORY MUST BE SUBMITTED TO THE ENGINEER FOR FILING WITH THE \nBUILDING DEPARTMENT, NO CONCRETE SHALL BE PLACED WITHOUT THE DESIGN MIX BEING APPROVED BY THE \nBUILDING DEPARTMENT.\n4. CONCRETE STRENGTH SHALL BE AS FOLLOWS, UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED:\nA. PILE CAPS, GRADE BEAMS        \n4000 PSI AT 28 DAYS, STONE CONCRETE.\nB. POURED WALLS:\n4000 PSI AT 28 DAYS, STONE CONCRETE.\nC. SLAB ON GROUND\n4000 PSI AT 28 DAYS, STONE CONCRETE\n7. THE STRUCTURAL ENGINEER OR HIS FIELD QUALIFIED REPRESENTATIVE SHALL CHECK AND APPROVE ALL STEEL \nREINFORCEMENT PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL INCLUDE IN HIS BID THE COST OF 0.1 \nTONS OF ADDITIONAL REINFORCING STEEL, INCLUDING FABRICATION, BENDING, FURNISHING AND PLACING. THIS EXTRA \nSTOCK SHALL BE USED FOR SPECIAL CONDITIONS AS DIRECTED BY THE ARCHITECT, THE ARCHITECT'S AGENT OF THE \nOWNER'S CONSTRUCTION SUPERVISOR. THE COST OF ALL UN-USED EXTRA STOCK SHALL BE CREDITED TO THE \nOWNER'S ACCOUNT. \n8. REINFORCING SHALL BE ACCURATELY PLACED, RIGIDLY SUPPORTED AND FIRMLY TIED IN PLACE, WITH APPROPRIATE \nBAR SUPPORTS AND SPACERS. LAP CONTINUOUS REINFORCING THE GREATEST OF 48 BAR DIAMETER AND LAP SPLICE \nTABLES INDICATED ON DRAWING. LAP BOTTOM STEEL OVER SUPPORTS AND TOP STEEL AT MIDSPAN (UNO). HOOK \nDISCONTINUOUS ENDS OF ALL TOP BARS AND ALL BARS IN WALLS (UNO). PROVIDE COVER REINFORCING AS FOLLOWS:\nA.       ELEMENTS\n                               BOTTOM\nTOP\nSIDE\na. FOOTINGS                                                    3\"                 2\"                 3\"\nb. BEAMS ABOVE GRADE                             1-1/2\"\n       1-1/2\"\n      1-1/2\"\nc. \nCOLUMNS                                                     -                   -              1-1/2\"\nd. SLABS ON GRADE                                      3\"                 1\"                  2\"\ne. SLABS ABOVE GRADE                                3/4\"\n        3/4\"                1\"\nf. \nSLABS EXPOSED TO WEATHER\n        1-1/2\"\n       1-1/2\"\n       1-1/2\"\ng. WALLS RETAINING FILL                             -                  -                  3\"\nh. WALLS ABOVE GRADE                                 -                   -                 3/4\"\n9. ALL SPLICES SHALL BE LAPPED IN ACCORDANCE WITH ACI 318. THE LOCATIONS SHALL BE INDICATED ON THE SHOP \nDRAWINGS AND APPROVED BY THE ENGINEER OF RECORD. GENERALLY, ALL SPLICES SHALL BE STAGGERED AND \nLOCATED AWAY FROM THE SECTION OF MAXIMUM TENSILE STRESS. ALL REINFORCEMENT SHALL BE ACCURATELY \nPLACED AND SECURELY WIRED TO PREVENT DISLOCATION FROM PROPER POSITION. PROVIDE CHAIRS FOR SUPPORT \nOF ALL REINFORCEMENTS. LIFTING OF BARS OR MESH DURING PLACEMENT OF CONCRETE IS NOT PERMITTED.\n10. VERTICAL CONSTRUCTION JOINTS IN ALL WALLS SHALL BE LOCATED AT LEAST 4'-0\" FROM ANY SUPPORTING COLUMN \nOR WALL OPENING. THE DISTANCE BETWEEN JOINTS IN A WALL SHALL BE AS PER SPECS. HORIZONTAL JOINTS IN \nWALLS, OTHER THAN THOSE DETAILED, SHOULD BE AVOIDED UNLESS UNAVOIDABLE, ADDITIONAL REINFORCING \nREQUIRED IN SUCH CASES SHALL BE AS DIRECTED BY THE ENGINEER AT NO COST TO THE CLIENT. NO HORIZONTAL \nJOINTS WILL BE ALLOWED IN GRADE BEAMS.\n11. THE CONTRACTOR IS TO INSTALL ALL PIPE SLEEVES, BOXED OPENINGS, ANCHOR BOLTS, ETC., AS REQUIRED FOR THE \nVARIOUS TRADES. WALL POCKETS TO RECEIVE BEAMS AND SLABS SHALL BE PROVIDED AS REQUIRED FOR THE \nSUPERSTRUCTURE. SHOP DRAWINGS SHOWING POSITION OF OPENINGS SHALL BE SUBMITTED TO THE STRUCTURAL \nENGINEER PRIOR TO PLACING CONCRETE. ALL LOCATIONS ARE TO BE OBTAINED FROM \"MEP\" AND ARCHITECTURAL \nDRAWINGS.\n12. DO NOT INCREASE QUANTITY OF WATER IN EXCESS OF THAT ESTABLISHED BY DESIGN MIX. IF LOSS OF SLUMP OCCURS \nBECAUSE OF THE USE OF FIBERMESH; ADD SUPERPLASTICIZER IN ACCORDANCE WITH CONCRETE SUPPLIERS QUALITY \nCONTROL PERSONEL.\n13. WHEN MEAN-DAILY-TEMPERATURE RISES ABOVE 90F, PROVIDE HOT WEATHER PROTECTION IN ACCORDANCE WITH \nACI-305. WHEN MEAN-DAILY-TEMPERATURE FALLS BELOW 40F, PROVIDE COLD WEATHER PROTECTION IN ACCORDANCE \nWITH ACI 306. SUBMIT PROPOSED METHODS FOR COLD AND/OR HOT WEATHER CONCRETING FOR REVIEW.\n14. DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION OF FORMWORK IS TO COMPLY WITH THE ACI CODE. PROVIDE ╛\" CHAMFER FOR ALL \nEXPOSED CORNERS.\n15. WHERE NO REINFORCEMENT IS SPECIFIED ON DRAWINGS, PROVIDE MINIMUM TEMPERATURE REINFORCEMENT IN \nACCORDANCE WITH ACI-318; BUT, NOT LESS THAN #4 REBARS AT 16\" ON CENTER.\n16. WHEN INSTALLING EXPANSION BOLTS OR ADHESIVE ANCHORS, THE CONTRACTOR SHALL TAKE MEASURES TO AVOID \nDRILLING OR CUTTING OF ANY EXISTING REINFORCING AND DESTRUCTION OF THE CONCRETE. HOLES SHALL BE BLOWN \nCLEAN PRIOR TO PLACING BOLTS OR ADHESIVE ANCHORS.\n17. VOID FORMERS SHOWN ON THE STRUCTURAL DRAWINGS SHALL BE RIGID CLOSED CELL EXPANDED POLYSTYRENE \nCONFORMING TO ASTM C578. VOID FORMERS SHALL UNDERGO 10% DEFORMATION WHEN SUBJECTED TO THE \nFOLLOWING LOADS AS PER ASTM D1621.\nA. COMPRESSIBLE VOID FORMERS    5.0 PSI\nB. RIGID VOID FORMERS              \n25.0 PSI\n5. ALL STEEL REINFORCEMENT SHALL HAVE AN ULTIMATE TENSILE STRENGTH OF 90,000 PSI AS PER ASTM A615, GRADE 60. \nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL FURNISH AND INSTALL ALL THE NECESSARY CHAIRS, REBARS, TIES, SPACERS, ETC., TO \nSECURE AND SUPPORT THE REINF. WHILE PLACING THE CONCRETE. REINFORCING SHALL BE EPOXY COATED WHERE \nINDICATED IN THESE NOTES AND/OR ON PLANS.\n6. ALL DETAILING, FABRICATION AND ERECTION OF REINFORCING BARS SHALL COMPLY WITH THE REQUIREMENTS OF ACI \n315 AND ACI 318. THE CONTRACTOR MUST SUBMIT REINFORCING SHOP DRAWINGS TO THE STRUCTURAL ENGINEER FOR \nREVIEW. NO CONSTRUCTION IS TO BE STARTED UNTIL THE SHOP DRAWINGS ARE REVIEWED BY THE ENGINEER AND \nAPPROVED BY THE BUILDING DEPARTMENT.\n200 MADISON AVENUE, 14TH FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY 10016\n212-689-3110\nARRAY-ARCHITECTS.COM\nPROJECT NO.\nDATE\nCONTRACT NO.\nCON/REF NO.\nF\nE\nD\nC\nB\nA\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n3\n2\n1\nC  COPYRIGHT - 2021 ARRAY ARCHITECTS\nIN COLLABORATION WITH:\nDOSHI ENGINEERING PLLC\nMEP ENGINEER\n350 SEVENTH AVENUE, 15th FLOOR,\nNEW YORK, NY 10001\nPHONE: 718 896 9324\nPROJECT:\nISSUES:\nSEAL:\nKEYPLAN:\nYSRAEL A. SEINUK, P.C.\nSTRUCTURAL ENGINEER\n228 EAST 45TH STREET, 2ND FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY  10017\nPHONE: 212 687 2233\nYU & ASSOCIATES\nGEOTECHNICAL & CIVIL ENGINEER\n611 RIVER DRIVE\nELMWOOD PARK, NY  07407\nPHONE: 201 791 0057\nMG ENGINEERING D.P.C.\nMEDICAL EQ, AV/IT, SECURITY ENGINEER\n116 WEST 32ND STREET\nNEW YORK, NY  10001\nPHONE: 212 643 9055  \nENVIRONMENTAL PLANNING \nMANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER\n1983 MARCUS AVENUE, SUITE 109\nLAKE SUCCESS, NY  11042\nPHONE: 516 328 1194 \n9/24/2025 5:16:08 PM\nC:\\Users\\afitzgerald\\Documents\\6829-STRUCT- ED ADDITION-25_Fitz1024.rvt\nFO-002\nFOUNDATION\nGENERAL NOTES\nED Ambulance Bay\nAddition\nH+H Bellevue\n6829\n06/06/2022\n462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\nNO.\nDESCRIPTION\nDATE\n1\n95% Solution\n6/20/2025\nISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID     7/18/25\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052632435}}
{"type":"message","id":"903d3ba6","parentId":"d086f625","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:23.363Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've gathered a lot of information from the drawings and text files. Now let me analyze the key pages more carefully for specific MEP and specialty items. Let me also re-examine the construction plan to get accurate fixture counts.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me analyze the construction plan (A-101) more carefully to get accurate counts:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:35","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_026.png","prompt":"This is sheet A-101 Construction Plan. Count EXACT quantities of: 1) Plumbing fixtures (water closets, urinals, lavatories, sinks, drinking fountains), 2) Fire extinguisher cabinets, 3) Toilet compartments/stalls, 4) Visual display boards or monitors, 5) Signage, 6) Any security equipment symbols, 7) Fire alarm devices. Provide specific counts with room locations."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:36","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_039.png","prompt":"This is an HVAC/mechanical plan. Identify and count: 1) HVAC equipment (ACU, exhaust fans, unit heaters), 2) Diffusers and grilles, 3) Ductwork routing, 4) Thermostats/controls. Describe the HVAC scope for the ambulance bay addition."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:37","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_054.png","prompt":"This is a mechanical/HVAC plan. Identify: 1) ACU-1 air conditioning unit details, 2) Ductwork sizes and routing, 3) Exhaust fans, 4) Any ventilation equipment. Provide equipment specifications if shown."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"moonshot","model":"kimi-k2.5","usage":{"input":68169,"output":388,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":68557,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770052632437}}
{"type":"message","id":"7ff0274e","parentId":"903d3ba6","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:30.986Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:35","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is **not** sheet A-101 (a Construction/Floor Plan). This is a **COMcheck Envelope Compliance Certificate and Inspection Checklist** — an energy code compliance document. It contains no architectural floor plans, fixture symbols, or equipment layouts.\n\n**All counts are zero:**\n\n1. **Plumbing fixtures:** 0\n2. **Fire extinguisher cabinets:** 0\n3. **Toilet compartments/stalls:** 0\n4. **Visual display boards/monitors:** 0\n5. **Signage:** 0\n6. **Security equipment:** 0\n7. **Fire alarm devices:** 0\n\nThis sheet contains only envelope assembly tables (walls, roofs, doors, windows with R-values/U-factors), an inspection checklist, and project information for the **H+H Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition** by Array Architects."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_026.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052650981}}
{"type":"message","id":"9856dd9a","parentId":"7ff0274e","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:40.056Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:36","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is **not an HVAC/mechanical plan** — it is sheet **E-401.00, \"Electrical Details 1\"** for the ED Ambulance Bay Addition project (H+H Bellevue).\n\nThe sheet contains **electrical details only**:\n\n- Typical device mounting heights\n- Wall-mounted low voltage outlet installation detail\n- Low voltage wiring installation detail\n- Conduit roof penetration detail\n- Conduit penetration thru fire-rated concrete slab\n- Cable penetration thru fire-rated gypsum wallboard/stud wall assembly\n- Occupancy sensor wiring diagrams (single-zone and two-zone)\n- Automatic-on/off operation wall-mounted occupancy sensor wiring diagram\n\n**There are no HVAC components on this sheet** — no ACUs, exhaust fans, unit heaters, diffusers, grilles, ductwork, or thermostats are shown. The HVAC scope would be found on mechanical sheets (typically M-series drawings)."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_039.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052660049}}
{"type":"message","id":"830d5774","parentId":"9856dd9a","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:58.193Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:37","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Mechanical Details Sheet M-304.00 — H+H Bellevue ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\nThis is a **mechanical details sheet** (4 of 9), not a floor plan. It shows standard construction details rather than equipment schedules or routing layouts. Here's what's depicted:\n\n## 1) ACU-1 Air Conditioning Unit\n- **Not shown on this sheet.** No ACU-1 details or schedules appear.\n\n## 2) Ductwork Details\n- **Fire and Smoke Damper Detail** — Shows damper sleeve construction, dual heat sensor/firestat, smoke detector, flex conduit, access door, connecting rod/link, and rated partition penetration requirements. Damper sleeves sized per gauge: 0\"-30\" = 24GA, 31\"-54\" = 22GA, 55\"-96\" = 20GA, over 96\" = 16GA.\n- **Linear Diffuser Detail** — 12\"x12\" plenum (or as shown on plans), 4\"-0\" on centers max, flex duct connection with volume damper, 6\" min spacing.\n- **Branch Duct Volume Damper Detail** — Shows splitter type dampers, single leaf dampers, 16GA blades, locking quadrant regulators. For ducts >48\" use multi-blade or opposed-action dampers.\n- **Supply Branch Duct with Splitter Type Damper** — Trunk duct to branch duct, 16GA base length, clinch connection on all sides.\n- **Supply Air Split Connection with Splittler Damper**\n\n## 3) Exhaust Fans\n- **Not shown on this sheet.**\n\n## 4) Ventilation Equipment Details\n- **Heating Coil Connections w/2-Way Valve (Hot Water)** — Shows hot water supply/return, air vent, coil, bypass, 3/4\" drain, control valve. All reducers shall be eccentric type.\n- **Combination flow measuring/balancing valve up to 2-1/2\"**; 3\" and above use plug valve & separate flow meter (Barco).\n\n## General Notes\n1. Dampers to be UL labeled, N"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_054.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052678187}}
{"type":"message","id":"8492c221","parentId":"830d5774","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:18:17.747Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I got some useful information from the mechanical details sheet. Let me look at the actual A-101 construction plan and find more specific information about plumbing fixtures, fire protection, and other specialty items.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:38","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_011.png","prompt":"This is sheet A-101 First Floor Plan. Count EXACT quantities of: 1) Plumbing fixtures (toilets, sinks, lavatories, drinking fountains), 2) Fire extinguisher cabinets/symbols, 3) Toilet compartments/stalls with partitions, 4) Any signage symbols, 5) Security equipment or cameras, 6) Fire alarm devices (smoke detectors, pull stations, horns). List counts by room name."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:39","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_042.png","prompt":"This is a Fire Alarm plan. Count all fire alarm devices: 1) Smoke detectors, 2) Heat detectors, 3) Pull stations (manual fire alarm boxes), 4) Fire alarm horns/strobes, 5) Fire alarm control panels. Provide device locations by room/area."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:40","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_051.png","prompt":"This is a plumbing plan. Count all plumbing fixtures: 1) Water closets/toilets, 2) Lavatories/sinks, 3) Floor drains, 4) Hose bibbs, 5) Any other plumbing fixtures. Provide fixture locations by room name."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"moonshot","model":"kimi-k2.5","usage":{"input":69403,"output":369,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":69772,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopRe