{"type":"message","id":"3cc19597","parentId":"33a0ba45","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:18:47.737Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read:42","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ZONING ANALYSIS\nBUILDING DEPARTMENT NOTES\nFIRE RATINGS\nSPECIAL INSPECTIONS\nCODE REQUIREMENTS FOR RENOVATIONS\nFLOOD AREA CALCULATIONS                                             (AS DEFINED IN ART. I,CH. 2 SECT. 12-10 NYCZR)\nTO BE REVISED FOR ED ENTRY\nLEVEL                                                   \nNEW GROSS \nFLOOR AREA\nNEW ZONING GROSS \nFLOOR AREA\nCELLAR LEVEL\n------                                                                 -----\nGROUND FL.  (ACTUAL 1ST FLOOR)            454 SF                                                          454 SF\nMEZANNINE FL.  \n   \n              ------                                                                ------   \nFIRST FL.   (ACTUAL 2ND FLOOR)                  ------                                                                ------   \nSECOND FL.  (ACTUAL 3RD FLOOR)             394 SF                                                           394  SF\nTOTAL\n    \n848 SF\n848 SF\nEXISTING ZONING GROSS FLOOR\nAREA FOR BELLEVUE CAMPUS                                                                                          3,266,855 SF\nFLOOR AREA (F.A.R.) CALCULATIONS (PER SECT. 24-11 NYCZR) FOR COMMUNITY IN R-8 DISTRICT:\nALLOWABLE F.A.R .                           1,045,440 X 6.5 = 6,795,360                                            6.50\nEXISTING F.A.R.                                  3,266,855/1,045,440 =3.13                                          < 6.50\nNEW F.A.R                \n              3,267,703/1,045,440 =3.13                                          < 6.50\nMAXIMUM PERMITTED LOT COVERAGE (PER SECT. 24-11 NYCZR FOR CORNER LOT IN R-8 DISTRICT)\n( 1,045,440 SF X  0.75 )                                                                                                          784,080 SF\nEXISTING COVERAGE                                                                                                          313,674 SF\nNEW COVERAGE\n314,118 SF\nEGRESS NOTES \nALL EGRESS REQUIREMENTS SHALL COMPLY WITH 27-357 TABLE 6.1.\nALL EXITS SHALL BE KEPT READILY ACCESSIBLE AND UNOBSTRUCTED AT ALL TIMES \nIN CONFORMANCE WITH SECTION 27-370.\n  \nINTERIOR DOORS TO COMPLY WITH 27-371C.\nCORRIDORS ARE TO COMPLY WITH ALL APPLICABLE REQUIREMENTS OF 27-369 \nINCLUDING THE FOLLOWING: \nIN H-3 OCCUPANCIES CORRIDORS MAY BE CONSTRUCTED OF UNRATED \nNONCOMBUSTIBLE MATERIAL IN THE FOLLOWING INSTANCES:  NURSES STATIONS \nNOT EXCEEDING 350 SF, WAITING SPACES, RECEPTION AND RECREATION AREAS \nFOR PATIENTS AND VISITORS NOT EXCEEDING 500 SF AND ALL OTHER SPACES \nCOMPLETELY PROTECTED BY AUTOMATIC SPRINKLERS AS COMPLYING WITH S.C. 17. \nNO DOOR OPENING INTO THE STAIR ABOVE THE ENTRANCE STORY SHALL BE HUNG \nSO AS TO REDUCE THE REQUIRED CLEAR WIDTH OF THE STAIR OR STAIR \nPLATFORM TO LESS THAN 75% OF THE REQUIRED WIDTH OR TO LESS THAN THE \nDOOR WIDTH OPENING UPON THEM\nSMOKE-STOP DOORS TO COMPLY WITH 27-371.C.\nIN H-2 OCCUPANCIES CORRIDORS SHALL BE DIVIDED BY SMOKE BARRIERS AT \n150’-0”.\nDEAD END CORRIDORS PER 27-369D SHALL NOTEXCEED THE LENGHT IN TABLE 6-1,\nH-2 30 FEET\nEXIT DOORS  ARE TO COMPLY WITH ALL APPLICABLE REQUIREMENTS OF 27-371A\nINCLUDING THE FOLLOWING: \nDOORS FOR REQUIRED EXITS ARE TO BE SELF-CLOSING WITH A 1 ½ HOUR\nFIRE PROTECTION RATING, EXCEPT THAT EXTERIOR STREET FLOOR EXIT DOORS \nHAVING AN EXTERIOR SEPARATION OF MORE THAN 15’ NEED NOT BE FIRE \nPROTECTED AND DOORS INTO STAIRS AND EXIT PASSAGEWAYS SHALL HAVE A \nMINIMUM FIRE PROTECTION RATING OF ¾ HOUR. \nALL EXIT DOORS ARE TO OPEN IN THE DIRECTION OF EGRESS. \nEXIT DOORS SHALL BE READILY OPERABLE AT ALL TIMES FROM THE SIDE\nFROM WHICH EGRESS IS TO BE MADE.  DOORS OPENING ONTO INTERIOR \nENCLOSED STAIRS SHALL NOT BE LOCKED FROM EITHER SIDE EXCEPT THAT DOORS \nMAY BE LOCKED TO PREVENT ACCESS TO THE STAIR FROM THE OUTSIDE AT \nSTREET LEVEL. \nFLOOR LEVELS ON BOTH SIDES OF ALL EXIT AND CORRIDOR DOORS ARE TO BE \nLEVEL AND AT THE SAME ELEVATION FOR A DISTANCE AT LEAST EQUAL TO THE \nWIDTH OF THE DOOR. \nALL EXIT LIGHTING SHALL COMPLY WITH 27-381.\nALL EXITS AND THEIR ACCESS FACILITIES SHALL BE EQUIPPED WITH ADEQUATE \nARTIFICIAL LIGHTING (MINIMUM OF 5 FOOT CANDLES AT FLOOR LEVEL), IN \nCONTINUOUS OPERATION.  EXIT LIGHTING SHALL BE CONNECTED TO AN \nEMERGENCY POWER SOURCE OR TO STORAGE BATTERY EQUIPMENT THAT IS \nAPPROVED BY THE BUREAU OF ELECTRICAL CONTROL. \nEXIT SIGNS ARE TO BE PROVIDED AS REQUIRED, PER 27-383 - 27-387.  LOCATION OF \nEVERY EXIT ON EVERY FLOOR SHALL BE CLEARLY INDICATED BY EXIT SIGNS.  \nDIRECTIONAL SIGNS ARE TO BE INSTALLED TO SERVE AS A GUIDE FROM ALL \nPORTIONS OF THE CORRIDOR FLOOR.  EXIT SIGNAGE SHALL BE CONNECTED TO AN \nEMERGENCY POWER SOURCE OR TO STORAGE BATTERY EQUIPMENT THAT IS \nAPPROVED BY THE BUREAU OF ELECTRICAL CONTROL. SIGNS SHALL BE \nINTERNALLY LIGHTED, HAVING AN INITIAL BRIGHTNESS OF LETTERS OF AT LEAST 25 \nFEET LAMBERT. \nDEMOLITION SEQUENCE PROCEDURE:\nDEMOLITION TO BE SEQUENCED FLOOR BY FLOOR AND WILL BEGIN FROM THE TOP \nFLOOR AND END AT THE LOWER FLOOR.\nCONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN SERVICE SYSTEMS, LIFE SAFETY SYSTEMS AND \nEQUIPMENT AND WILL REMAIN ACTIVE AND IN OPERATION DURING DEMOLITION.\nEXISTING BUILDING ACCESS COMPLY WITH 27-292.\nFIRE DEPARTMENT ACCESS COMPLY WITH 27-292A.\nACCESSIBILITY ACCESS COMPLY WITH 27-292.5: \nTHE PRIMARY ENTRANCE(S) OF THE EXISTING BUILDING IS ACCESSIBLE FOR PEOPLE \nHAVING PHYSICAL DISABILITIES.  EXTERIOR AND INTERIOR ROUTES ARE PROVIDED. \nFIRE DIVISION COMPLY WITH 27-232: \nVERTICAL OR HORIZONTAL CONSTRUCTION, PROVIDING THE REQUIRED FIRE BARRIER \nBETWEEN ADJOINING BUILDINGS OR ADJOINING OR SUPERIMPOSED FIRE AREAS OR \nBUILDING SECTIONS. \nNUMBER OF EXITS TO COMPLY WITH  27-365. \nEXITS FROM FLOOR TO COMPLY WITH 27-366.\nAT LEAST TWO INDEPENT EXIT REMOTE FROM EACH OTHER FROM EVERY FLOOR. \nFROM ROOM OR SPACE TO COMPLY WITH 27-365.\nAT LEAST TWO DOOR REQUIRED IF THE OCCUPANT LOAD EXCEEDS THE NUMBER OF \nPEOPLE IN TABLE 6-3.\nEXIT COMPLY WITH 27-367: \nFLOOR AREA HAVING ACCESS TO AREA OF REFUGE, THE NUMBER OF PERSONS FOR \nWHOM VERTICAL EXITS ARE REQUIRED MAY BE REDUCED BY 50% OF OCCUPANT LOAD \nWHEN ONE AREA OF REFUGE IS PROVIDED.  WHEN TWO AREAS ARE PROVIDED, REDUCE \nBY 33%. \nEXIT COMPLY WITH 27-232: \nA MEANS OF EGRESS FROM AN INTERIOR OF A BUILDING WHICH IS PROVIDED BY USE OF \nTHE FOLLOWING, EITHER SINGULARLY OR IN COMBINATION: VERTICAL EXITS, EXIT \nPASSAGEWAYS, HORIZONTAL EXITS, INTERIOR STAIRS, EXTERIOR STAIRS. \nHORIZ. EXIT COMPLY WITH 27-373: \nA HORIZONTAL EXIT TO AN AREA OF REFUGE MAY CONSIST OF DOORS THROUGH WALLS \nOR PARTITIONS HAVING AT LEAST TWO (2) HOUR FIRE RESISTANCE RATING.\nEXIT PASSAGEWAYS TO COMPLY WITH 27-370.\nCORRIDORS AND EXIT PASSAGEWAYS SHALL HAVE A CLEAR HEIGHT OF 7'-6\" FOR AT \nLEAST 75% OF THE FLOOR AREA WITH NO POINT LESS THAN 7'-0\" IN HEIGHT. PROJECTION \nBELOW THE CEILING SHALL NOT OBSTRUCT FULL VIEW OF EXIT SIGNS, 27-369 (b).\nAREA REFUGE COMPLY WITH 27-232: \nFLOOR AREA TO WHICH EGRESS IS MADE THROUGH A HORIZONTAL EXIT. \nAREA REFUGE COMPLY WITH 27-372: \nIS TO COMPLY WITH THE FOLLOWING:(A) TWO HOUR\nFIRE RESISTANT SEPARATION (B) HOLD OCCUPANT LOAD IT RECEIVES (FROM FLOOR \nAREA COMPUTED AS OF 27-367) PLUS ITS OWN OCCUPANT LOAD.  ALLOWING \n3 SF/P.  INPATIENT AREAS OF H-2 OCCUPANCY;  THE ALLOWANCE IS 30 SF/P.  (C) AT \nLEAST ONE VERTICAL EXIT WILL SUPPLY EACH AREA OF REFUGE. \nAN INTERIOR SPACE THAT SERVES AS A MANES OF EGRESS BY PROVIDING A \nTRANSITIONAL AREA FROM (AND THAT ALSO SERVES AS A NORMAL MEANS OF ENTRY \nTO) AN ASSEMBLY SPACE. \nEXITS FROM SAFE AREAS COMPLY WITH (6): \nTHE CAPACITY OF EXITS FROM SAFE AREAS SHALL BE LISTED IN TABLE 8-1.  THE EXIT \nOPENINGS FROM SAFE ARES SHALL DISCHARGE INTO EXIT TYPES AS PROVIDED IN \nSUBCHAPTER SIX (TABLE 6-1). \nDETERMINATION OF EXIT REQUIREMENTS SHALL COMPLY WITH 27-357 AND TABLE 6-1.\nEXIT CAPACITY TO COMPLY WITH 27-359.\nOCCUPANCY LOAD TO COMPLY WITH 27-358, TABLE 6.2.\nH-2 : INSTITUTIONAL ADULTS SLEEPING ROOMS 75 SQ. FT. NET \nH-2 : STAFF AREAS 30 SQ. FT. NET\nMAXIMUM TRAVEL DISTANCE TO COMPLY WITH 27-360 AND TABLE 6-1\nH-2: TRAVEL DISTANCE (SPRINKLER) IS 175 FT.  TO STAIRS, EXIT PASSAGEWAYS, \nHORIZONTAL EXITS.  \nF-1B- ASSEMBLY AREAS TO COMPLY WITH TABLE 8-1: \nTRAVEL DISTANCE (PRIMARY) IS 100 FT.  TO STAIRS, SAFE AREAS, EXIT PASSAGEWAYS \nSTAIR AND ELEVATOR SIGNS TO COMPLY WITH 27-390, 27-396.\nNO CHANGE IN OVERALL BUILDING OCCUPANCY GROUP (H-2), \nWITH AN EXTENSION OF 2ND FLOOR (ACTUAL 3RD FLOOR)\nCOMPLY WITH TABLE 3-1: \nFIRE INDEX:\n1 \nCOMPLY WITH TABLE 4-1: FOR A SPRINKLERED, CLASS I-A BUILDING \nMAX. AREA = NO LIMIT, MAX. HEIGHT = NO LIMIT \nNO CHANGE IN BUILDING CONSTRUCTION TYPE GROUP I-A NONCOMBUSTIBLE \nCOMPLY WITH TABLE 3-4:\nREQUIRED\nPROVIDED\nU.L#\nNONBEARING EXTERIOR WALL\n0 HR.\n0 HR.\n--\nINTERIOR BEARING WALL\n4 HR.\nN/A\nN/A\nENCLOSE. OF VERT. EXITS, EXIT\nPASSAGEWAYS, SHAFTS\n2 HR.\n2 HR.\nU438\nCOLUMNS, GIRDERS, TRUSSES \n(MORE THAN 1 FLR)\n4 HR.\n4 HR.\nX325\nFLOOR CONSTRUCTION\n3 HR.\n3 HR.\nD660\nROOF CONSTRUCTION\n2 HR.\n2 HR.\nD626\nBEAM\n3 HR.\n3 HR.\nN728\nALL WORK SHALL BE PERFORMED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE NEW YORK CITY BUILDING \nCONSTRUCTION CODE AND THE RULES AND REGULATIONS OF ALL AGENCIES, \nDEPARTMENTS AND COMMISSIONS HAVING JURISDICTION.\nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL, PRIOR TO THE COMMENCEMENT OF WORK, SECURE ALL \nREQUIRED AND NECESSARY PERMITS, APPROVALS, ETC.  FROM ALL MUNICIPAL AGENCIES \nAND RESPECTIVE DEPARTMENTS HAVING JURISDICTION AT THE COST AND EXPENSE OF \nTHE CONTRACTOR AND PRIOR TO START OF WORK AS REQUIRED BY N.Y.C. BUILDING \nCODE.\nNOTICE OF COMMENCEMENT OF WORK TO COMPLY WITH SECTION 27-195.\nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROTECT ALL ADJACENT AND EXISTING SIDEWALKS, CURBS, \nSHRUBS, ETC. AND SHALL REPAIR AND RESTORE, TO PRE-CONSTRUCTION CONDITION \nAND TO THE OWNER'S SATISFACTION, ALL SUCH FEATURES DAMAGED DURING \nCONSTRUCTION OPERATION AS PER SECTION 27-1026-27-1030.\nSAFETY OF PUBLIC AND PROPERTY DURING CONSTRUCTION TO COMPLY WITH ARTICLE 7 \nOF TITLE   26, SUBCHAPTER 3 AND CHAPTER 16 OF APPENDIX A.    \nHUNG AND FURRED CEILING OR SOFFITS, CONCEALING HEATING, PLUMBING OR \nELECTRICAL WORK SHALL NOT BE BUILT UNTIL SUCH WORK IS INSTALLED OR TESTED.\nCEILING TO CONFORM WITH 27-327, 27-345.\n  \nA PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER LICENSED IN THE STATE OF NEW YORK SHALL BE REQUIRED \nBY THE OWNER TO PERFORM THE INSPECTIONS AS REQUIRED BY 27-132.\nINTERIOR FIRE ALARM AND SIGNAL SYSTEM TO COMPLY WITH 27-968 ~ 27-977.\nPROVIDE ELECTRICALLY FIRE ALAM SINNAL SYSTEM.\nFIRE DIVISIONS TO COMPLY WITH 27-340, TABLE 5.2.\nFIRE SEPARATION TO COMPLY WITH 27-341, TABLE 5.1.\nANY OPENING IN FIRE DIVISIONS AND/OR FIRE SEPARATION SHALL COMPLY WITH SECTION \n27-342.\nALL PENETRATIONS OR RECESSED OPENINGS IN WALLS, PARTITIONS, OR FLOOR SLABS \nSHALL MAINTAIN THE REQUIRED FIRE RATING.\nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE FIRESTOPPING AT ALL FLOOR AND RATED WALL \nPENETRATIONS, REFERENCE SPECIFICATIONS FOR APPROVED MATERIALS.\nALL FIRE RESISTANT REQUIREMENTS SHALL COMPLY WITH 27-323-27-330.\nALL FIRE STOPPING SHALL COMPLY WITH 27-345.\nANY REQUIRED WOOD BLOCKING OR WOOD USED IN THE FABRICATION OF ANY FIXED \nCONSTRUCTION WITHIN THE PROJECT SHALL BE FIRE-RETARDANT TREATED IN \nCONFORMANCE WITH SECTION 27-328.\nALL MATERIALS SHALL COMPLY WITH 27-131 FOR ACCEPTANCE.\nSTATEMENTS AND REPORTS OF INSPECTION SHALL BE SUBMITTED AS PER 27-212.\nALL CONCRETE BLOCKS FOR INTERIOR WYTHES OF EXTERIOR WALL AND WHERE NOTED \nFOR ELEVATOR SHAFTS SHALL BE 75% SOLID.\nALL UNIT MASONRY MATERIALS SHALL CONFORM TO THE REQUIREMENTS OF RS10-1, S3\nALL UNIT MASONRY PARTITIONS SHALL BE BONDED IN ACCORDANCE WITH RS10-1, S7\nINSPECTION REQUIREMENT FOR MATERIAL COMPLY WITH 27-132\nINTERIOR FINISHES TO COMPLY WITH 27-348.\nFINISHED FLOORING TO COMPLY WITH (b) 27-351.\nSpecial Inspection Items Code/Section\nSPRAYED 